OL,3,GNEWSALost village reappears as drought
OL,4,Acontinues
OL,5,
OL,6,FLow water levels at a reservoir in
OL,7,FDerbyshire have revealed a former
OL,8,Fsettlement that was deluged in the
OL,9,F1940s.
OL,11,FThe village of Derwent made way for
OL,12,FLadybower Reservoir, which was built
OL,13,Fbetween 1935 and 1943.
OL,15,FFigures show the reservoir's water
OL,16,Flevels stand at just under 32% capacity
OL,17,Ffollowing a sustained summer dry spell
OL,18,Fthat led to a drought being declared in
OL,19,Fthe East Midlands in August.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
